In Telangana land records, particularly in an Encumbrance Certificate (EC), the abbreviations PL, CL, and EX mean: 
PL: Principal (in the case of a Power of Attorney deed, the person transferring the land rights without necessarily taking money).
CL: Claimant (the person receiving the property or laying claim to it, typically the buyer).
EX: Executant (the person giving or selling the property, typically the owner/seller). 
